        "v": 1,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "part": "word/document.xml",
        "body_index": 128
      }
    },
    "text": "The fundamental difference lies in the sufficiency of physical facility. For an animal, adequate physical conditions (food, shelter, safety) are enough for survival and contentment. A human, however, requires more: along with physical comfort, humans need meaningful relationships and a correct understanding of themselves. These additional dimensions allow humans to achieve holistic development, transforming from an animal consciousness to a human consciousness.",
    "style_clone_from": {
      "adapter": "docx",
      "payload": {
        "v": 1,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "part": "word/document.xml",
