      "payload": {
        "v": 1,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "part": "word/document.xml",
        "body_index": 138
      }
    },
    "text": "Living with animal consciousness means living solely for physical facilities; the animal\u2019s life revolves around basic survival and physical comfort, which is largely adequate. Living with human consciousness, by contrast, requires the presence of three elements in the correct priority: first, right understanding in the self; second, fulfilment in relationships with other human beings; third, provision of physical facilities. When these three are integrated in that priority order, a being attains human consciousness, marking the shift toward holistic development.",
    "style_clone_from": {
      "adapter": "docx",
      "payload": {
        "v": 1,
